        },
        {
          "path": "_m/w/s/n/3/ludao-lighthouse-wp/green-island-lighthouse-1.jpg",
          "filename": "Green Island Lighthouse-1.jpg",
          "caption": "Green Island Lighthouse\nThe origin of the Green Island Lighthouse came from a shipwreck. In 1937, the most luxurious cruise ship, the President Hoover, was mistaken for the light of the Newport's successful lighthouse as a goose nose. The lighthouse caused the cruise ship to hit the reef outside the Green Island Mansion. The enthusiastic and friendly Green Island residents naturally assisted in the rescue. More than 1,100 passengers and crew members on the cruise ship were safely rescued, and they played the unique human touch of the islanders and enthusiastically let them These settled guests are placed at home, and the friendliness and enthusiasm of the island make all the people feel like spring breeze.\nIn the following year, the American Red Cross Society felt the shipwreck of President Hoover. In order to commemorate the shipwreck and strengthen the safety of sailing on the sea, donated money to build the Green Island Lighthouse, so that the northwest of the Green Island is deep in the sea. At night, for the lost ship, a light guide to the lost.\n\nThe Green Island Lighthouse Tower is 33.3 meters high and the tower is 150 steps. Stepping up to the high point of the lighthouse park overlooking the whole island, overlooking the ocean, the lighthouse, and not only guiding the sea vessels without getting lost, but also symbolizing the islanders’ volunteer rescue of the shipwreck, which was raised by the people on the Hoover President. The light of life.",
          "alt": "Green Island Lighthouse\nThe origin of the Green Island Lighthouse came from a shipwreck. In 1937, the most luxurious cruise ship, the President Hoover, was mistaken for the light of the Newport's successful lighthouse as a goose nose. The lighthouse caused the cruise ship to hit the reef outside the Green Island Mansion. The enthusiastic and friendly Green Island residents naturally assisted in the rescue. More than 1,100 passengers and crew members on the cruise ship were safely rescued, and they played the unique human touch of the islanders and enthusiastically let them These settled guests are placed at home, and the friendliness and enthusiasm of the island make all the people feel like spring breeze.\nIn the following year, the American Red Cross Society felt the shipwreck of President Hoover. In order to commemorate the shipwreck and strengthen the safety of sailing on the sea, donated money to build the Green Island Lighthouse, so that the northwest of the Green Island is deep in the sea. At night, for the lost ship, a light guide to the lost.\n\nThe Green Island Lighthouse Tower is 33.3 meters high and the tower is 150 steps. Stepping up to the high point of the lighthouse park overlooking the whole island, overlooking the ocean, the lighthouse, and not only guiding the sea vessels without getting lost, but also symbolizing the islanders’ volunteer rescue of the shipwreck, which was raised by the people on the Hoover President. The light of life.",
